description:
In app.js startEventSource() (lines 504-517), the EventSource onerror handler (line 513) logs a warning but does NOT crash or try to manually reconnect:

  eventsource.onerror = () => {
    console.warn('Kith EventSource: connection lost, will reconnect');
  };

The browser's EventSource handles reconnection automatically with exponential backoff per the spec. Trying to manually reconnect would be redundant and could cause exponential backoff to be defeated.

The logging is helpful for debugging but non-blocking. This pattern is correct: let the platform handle transient network faults.

Alternative (throw, crash, or force-reconnect) would be worse.
